{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/pulls/997","id":4248584229,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSbOoU879PEAl","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/997","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/997.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/997.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/997","number":997,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"A step to Formal AI being able to code itself, via Hive Mind (#996)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nA step toward the #996 self-coding loop: the most critical open issues (excluding those already executing in open PRs) are analyzed and fixed in this single PR, with the complete case study — collected Hive Mind session evidence, requirement decomposition, per-requirement solution plans, online research, and upstream reports — compiled under [`docs/case-studies/issue-996/`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-996-177371167e71/docs/case-studies/issue-996/README.md).\n\nFixes #996\nFixes #945\nFixes #956\nFixes #964\nFixes #979\n\n## What was fixed, with reproducing tests\n\n| Issue | Fix | Test |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| #956 | A formalization task that quotes its own source text («…», “…”, 「…」, 《…》) now formalizes that text instead of silently substituting the seeded «Сказка о рыбаке и рыбке» tale; a quoted *title* of the tale still selects the full canonical text. `FORMAL_AI_TRACE_REQUESTS=1` now also traces `agentic_task` / `formalization_source` routing. The recipe moved to `src/agentic_coding/formalization_recipe.rs` (file-size gate). | `tests/unit/issue_956.rs` (4 tests, en/ru/zh/hi) |\n| #945 | `Report`-flow harness/server log exports go to a surviving temp directory that prints its path, instead of dropping `formal-ai-*.lino` dumps into the caller's working directory. Also fixes machine-value report-target matching (`formal_ai` was dropped by prompt normalization). | `tests/unit/issue_945.rs` |\n| #979 | The Russian liveness probes «Ты тут?», «вы тут», «я тут» route to the `test_status` intent instead of falling through to a web search (pure seed data: `data/seed/intent-routing.lino`). Bare «тест», reported against v0.333.1, already routes correctly on current `main`. | `tests/unit/test_status.rs` extended matrix |\n| #964 | The 22 duplicate requirement IDs in `REQUIREMENTS.md` are renumbered to fresh unique IDs (issue-540 block → R537–R548, issue-657 R480 → R549, issue-674 block → R550–R558), with `docs/requirements-traceability.md` (collision preamble and `(Lxxxx)` suffixes removed), the issue-540 case study, guard tests, and the `ARCHITECTURE.md` ID range updated. | `tests/unit/docs_requirements_issue_540.rs`, `docs_requirements_issue_451.rs` |\n| hive-mind #2146 (R1c) | Final answers that inline machine text (general-change plan event, formalized knowledge base) wrap it in fenced `lino` code blocks so GitHub comments render it correctly. | `tests/unit/issue_996_markdown.rs` (3 tests) |\n\n## Hive Mind session-log analysis (hive-mind #2146)\n\nThree sanitized `solve` session logs are preserved under `docs/case-studies/issue-996/raw-data/` and analyzed line-by-line in the case study:\n\n- **Defect A — silent model substitution**: the `XOq3KX` session requested `--model formalai/formal-ai` but ran on `minimax-m2.5-free` (Bun/yargs argv bug, fail-open). Already reported and fixed upstream fail-closed in [agent#293](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/293) / [PR #294](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/294) (`js-0.25.8`); the machine-readable `model_resolved` attestation follow-up is [agent#295](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/295).\n- **Defect B — empty runs triggering auto-restart**: the `PhU3X2`/`8GWnaH` sessions ended with conversational filler and zero code changes. Formal-AI-side legs fixed here (#956 routing + routing trace); the restart-budget leg is Hive-Mind-side (R-B3 in hive-mind #2146).\n- **Defect C — collapsed markdown**: fixed by the fenced-block change above.\n\n## Not closed here, with recorded plans\n\n- #943 (unrequested issue filing): analyzed; the fix needs a negation lexicon in the seed plus a refusal path mirroring `protocol_policy.rs` — plan recorded in the case study so the issue can proceed independently.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --lib --bins --tests --all-features` (0 warnings), `rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs`, `rust-script scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs` — all green locally.\n- Full `cargo test --test unit` run on the merged tree.\n- Release trigger prepared via `changelog.d/20260810_996_report_flow_fixes.md` (patch bump).\n","created_at":"2026-08-10T22:03:44Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T07:08:02Z","closed_at":"2026-08-11T07:08:02Z","merged_at":"2026-08-11T07:08:02Z","merge_commit_sha":"42295418a6fd879affa92b49782d4ea9d8021e29","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.co